      "node_id": "kg_doc_12",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "USS \"Mahan\" (DLG-11/DDG-42), was a guided missile destroyer in the United States Navy. She was named for Rear Admiral Alfred Thayer Mahan USN (1840–1914). The ship was Laid down as DLG-11 by the San Francisco Naval Shipyard on 31 July 1957 and launched on 7 October 1959. \"Mahan\" was sponsored by Mrs. H. P. Smith, wife of Vice Adm. Harold Page Smith, and commissioned on 25 December 1960. \"Mahan\" was reclassified as a guided missile destroyer on 30 June 1975 and designated DDG-42. USS \"Mahan\" was decommissioned on 15 June 1993 and stricken from the Naval Vessel Register on the same day.",
      "depth": 0,
      "parent_id": null,
